meta {
  name: Create job - oversized body
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/jobs
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Oversized",
    "company": "Acme Corp",
    "description": "REPLACE ME with 50 KB+ of text to trip the body-size limit"
  }
}

docs {
  The BodySizeLimitMiddleware rejects any request body over 50 KB
  (MAX_BODY_BYTES = 51200 bytes) before it is parsed, counting the actual bytes
  streamed rather than trusting Content-Length.

  The body shipped here is a small placeholder, so as-is this request returns
  201, not 422. To trigger the 422 manually, paste 50 KB or more into the
  `description` field (e.g. duplicate a paragraph until the body exceeds 50 KB)
  and send again.

  Expected (body > 50 KB): 422 Unprocessable Entity
  Body: Pydantic-shaped envelope, detail[0].type = "too_large".

  This case is already covered by the automated pytest suite
  (tests/test_body_limit.py), including the streamed-in-chunks and
  lying-Content-Length variants, so exercising it here manually is optional.
}
